WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.760
What does a civil rights icon like Martin Luther King Jr.,

00:04.760 --> 00:08.500
a tech visionary like Steve Jobs, and a media mogul

00:08.500 --> 00:11.200
like Oprah Winfrey have in common?

00:11.200 --> 00:16.200
They all operate from a clear and powerful purpose.

00:16.700 --> 00:20.160
Your purpose is your why.

00:20.160 --> 00:23.380
It's your fundamental reason for being.

00:23.380 --> 00:25.140
Separate from your job title,

00:25.140 --> 00:28.500
it's the lasting impact you want to have.

00:28.500 --> 00:30.700
And it's what drives you to take action

00:30.700 --> 00:32.880
when the work gets hard.

00:32.880 --> 00:36.300
And yet, according to Harvard Business Review,

00:36.300 --> 00:38.920
fewer than 20% of leaders

00:38.920 --> 00:41.920
have a strong written purpose statement,

00:41.920 --> 00:44.660
and even fewer have written it down.

00:44.660 --> 00:49.660
But today, you join the elite 10%.

00:50.260 --> 00:51.880
But before we draft your own,

00:51.880 --> 00:56.580
it's critical to understand what purpose truly is.

00:56.580 --> 01:01.040
Think of your purpose as your personal operating system.

01:01.040 --> 01:05.960
It's the underlying code that runs everything else,

01:05.960 --> 01:10.960
your decisions, your actions, and your priorities.

01:11.360 --> 01:15.560
When the operating system is installed and running,

01:15.560 --> 01:18.860
you get powerful upgrades.

01:18.860 --> 01:23.480
The first is the greater meaning in your life and work.

01:23.480 --> 01:26.480
As an added bonus, research has shown

01:26.480 --> 01:30.060
that living your purpose can increase resiliency,

01:30.060 --> 01:33.460
improve sleep, and even decrease the risk

01:33.460 --> 01:35.540
of cardiac disease.

01:35.540 --> 01:37.740
But maybe the most powerful upgrade

01:37.740 --> 01:42.740
is how this OS manages your most valuable resource, time.

01:43.800 --> 01:46.500
Your purpose acts as a compass,

01:46.500 --> 01:49.740
guiding your time management towards a life

01:49.740 --> 01:53.700
that is not only efficient, but also fulfilling.

01:54.680 --> 01:57.940
It's the difference between doing things correctly,

01:57.940 --> 02:02.600
which is time management, and doing the right things,

02:02.600 --> 02:06.080
which is purpose-driven leadership.

02:11.600 --> 02:15.420
For me, my purpose is to awaken people

02:15.420 --> 02:18.640
to the power of purpose as a catalyst

02:18.640 --> 02:22.260
for remarkable leadership and a fulfilled life.

02:22.300 --> 02:26.620
When this why hit me, I had lost everything

02:26.620 --> 02:30.400
and struggled to keep this business alive.

02:30.400 --> 02:35.400
I would tell myself, this why is bigger than you, Melissa.

02:35.580 --> 02:38.800
Purpose can drive performance.

02:38.800 --> 02:41.540
You will go global, Melissa.

02:41.540 --> 02:46.220
And now, in over 26 countries and counting,

02:46.220 --> 02:50.680
those words on my vision board were not fluff,

02:50.700 --> 02:54.740
they were fuel, high octane, that is,

02:54.740 --> 02:59.660
that eventually connected you and I in this very moment.

02:59.660 --> 03:04.280
Notice, I didn't say I'm a CEO or I'm a coach.

03:04.280 --> 03:08.100
It's the why behind everything that I do.

03:08.100 --> 03:12.620
Knowing this why allows me to play to my strengths

03:12.620 --> 03:16.620
and clarify boundaries, ensuring I'm operating

03:16.620 --> 03:19.540
at my highest contribution.

03:19.560 --> 03:22.080
A financial leader I know describes her purpose

03:22.080 --> 03:26.060
as keeping my people from making short-sighted decisions

03:26.060 --> 03:28.980
against their own self-interest.

03:28.980 --> 03:32.240
It's about protection and wisdom.

03:32.240 --> 03:35.520
A brilliant engineer I coached said his purpose

03:35.520 --> 03:37.720
was to build elegant solutions

03:37.720 --> 03:41.560
that makes complex things simple for people.

03:41.560 --> 03:46.080
It's about creating clarity in a world of noise.

03:46.080 --> 03:48.680
In a world of constant change and distraction,

03:48.700 --> 03:52.140
your purpose is your anchor.

03:52.140 --> 03:53.820
It gives you stability.

03:53.820 --> 03:58.820
Having a clear purpose statement creates focus.

03:59.020 --> 04:03.180
It clarifies your choices and defines your priorities

04:03.180 --> 04:06.660
and defines how you operate each and every day.

04:06.660 --> 04:09.300
When you're faced with two good opportunities,

04:09.300 --> 04:13.060
your purpose statement is the tiebreaker.

04:13.060 --> 04:16.540
It tells you which path is truly yours.

04:17.440 --> 04:19.800
Now in your playbook, you'll find a drill

04:19.800 --> 04:22.760
designed to help you draft your purpose statement.

04:22.760 --> 04:25.320
Use the notes from lessons two,

04:25.320 --> 04:28.800
your values, the moments that moved you.

04:28.800 --> 04:33.420
This isn't about finding the perfect right words.

04:34.360 --> 04:37.280
It's about getting the first draft down.

04:37.280 --> 04:39.240
It's gotta feel authentic.

04:39.240 --> 04:42.080
It will take time and it's okay

04:42.080 --> 04:45.200
to have multiple drafts in this process.

04:45.200 --> 04:48.340
Choose progress over perfection.

